Description: qapi: Add a schema for the Chumby board
 A frontend for the chumby-classic machine shows what the guest does
 with the board's outputs (dims or blanks its view with the backlight
 and the LCD's power, shows the speaker as muted) and drives its inputs
 (headphones, the top button, the accelerometer). Polling for the
 outputs wastes wakeups.
 .
 Add qapi/chumby.json with query-chumby-state, returning the backlight
 level (the PWM's duty cycle, 0 to 65535), LCD power, speaker mute,
 headphones and button, the accelerometer's input (accel-x, accel-y and
 accel-z, in milli-g) and the device identity (guid, serial and
 hwversion), so that one command resynchronises a frontend; and the
 events CHUMBY_BACKLIGHT, CHUMBY_LCD, CHUMBY_SPEAKER_MUTE and
 CHUMBY_HEADPHONES. A backlight fade is many changes, so
 CHUMBY_BACKLIGHT is rate-limited to one each 100 ms, the last level
 always arriving. Machines without the board answer the query with an
 error, from a stub.
 .
 The schema is a module of its own, for the board's other controls to
 join.
